<title>USA: High Plains restarts York, Neb., plant.</title>
<headline>High Plains restarts York, Neb., plant.</headline>
<dateline>WICHITA, Kan. 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>High Plains Corp said it expected to restart operations at its York, Neb., ethanol-production plant on Thursday after a two-month shutdown.</p>
<p>It said it had halted production at the plant because of the high cost of grain.</p>
<p>High Plains said it used the downtime to repair and modify the facility, which currently produces fuel-grade ethanol. Beginning in January, it also turn out industrial-grade ethanol.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk, 312 408-8787</p>
